KAROTS SUITE — LICENCE AND SERVICE TERMS
Copyright (c) 2026 Karots Korp (Karots Dev). All rights reserved.

DRAFT for review by a Sri Lankan attorney-at-law before use. See docs/legal/README.md.

These terms are the body of the Licence and Service Agreement between Karots Korp, trading as
Karots Dev ("Karots", "we"), and the Shop named in it ("the Shop", "you"). With its Schedules
and the Shop Rules & Service Guide they are the whole agreement. If they conflict, the First
Schedule (Order Details) wins, then these terms, then the other Schedules, then the Guide.


1. DEFINITIONS

"Software" means Karots Suite as supplied to the Shop: the server program, the installer
(karots-setup), the plugins named in the Order Details, updates, and their documentation.
"Order Details" means the First Schedule to the agreement, signed (or electronically accepted),
which names the Shop, its site,
its install ID, the plugins, the fees and any services bought.
"Shop Data" means the records the Shop keeps in the Software: products, sales, stock, money,
customers, staff, patients and the like.
"Site" means the Shop's premises named in the Order Details.


2. ACCEPTANCE

2.1 You accept these terms by signing the agreement, or by ticking "I agree" or installing or
    using the Software. An electronic acceptance is as binding as a signed paper copy
    (Electronic Transactions Act, No. 19 of 2006, as amended by Act No. 25 of 2017).
2.2 You confirm you are taking the Software for a business, not as a private consumer.


3. LICENCE

3.1 Once the fees are paid, Karots gives you a non-exclusive, non-transferable licence to install
    and use the Software in machine-readable form, for the Shop's own business at the Site, on as
    many of the Shop's own computers there as it needs.
3.2 You may make the copies the law allows the lawful owner of a computer program: those needed
    to use it, and backup copies to replace a lost or damaged copy (Intellectual Property Act,
    No. 36 of 2003, section 12(7)). The Software's own backups of Shop Data are not limited by
    this clause.
3.3 Moving the Shop to another computer at the Site is allowed. Moving to another site, or a
    change of owner, needs Karots' written consent, which will not be refused without good
    reason. A change of owner carries the transfer fee in the Shop Rules & Service Guide, and the
    new owner signs new Order Details.


4. RESTRICTIONS

Except as the law expressly allows, you must not, and must not let anyone else:
(a) sell, resell, rent, lend, sublicense, share or distribute the Software, or use it for any
    other business or site;
(b) copy it beyond clause 3;
(c) reverse engineer, decompile or disassemble it, or try to obtain its source code;
(d) modify it, translate it or make works based on it;
(e) remove or change any copyright, licence or credit notice in it, on its screens or on what it
    prints;
(f) get around any licence check, install ID, support code, update signature or lock in it.
Breaking clause 4 may also be an offence under section 178 of the Intellectual Property Act.


5. OWNERSHIP

5.1 The Software is licensed, not sold. Karots owns all rights in it, including copyright in the
    programs, their design and documentation.
5.2 Open-source parts are under their own licences, listed in THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md. Nothing in
    these terms limits the rights those licences give you.


6. SHOP DATA

6.1 Shop Data belongs to the Shop. Karots claims no right to it and will not sell it.
6.2 The Shop decides what personal data it keeps (about customers, patients and staff) and why.
    It is the controller of that data, and Karots processes it only as the Third Schedule allows.
6.3 You can take a full backup of your Shop Data from the Software at any time, including after
    these terms end.


7. FEES

7.1 Fees, what they cover and when they are due are in the Order Details.
7.2 While a fee is late, Karots may pause updates, support, visits and Karots cloud backup until
    it is paid. The till keeps working, and Karots never locks the Shop out of its own Shop Data.
7.3 Any balance of the one-time price must be paid within 90 days of installation. If it is not,
    Karots will give written notice of 14 days. If the balance is still unpaid at the end of
    that notice, the licence ends under clause 11.2 and Karots may remove the Software, at the
    Site or remotely with the Shop's permission, after giving the Shop a full backup of its
    Shop Data. The Shop's rights in the Software are complete only when everything is paid.


8. UPDATES AND SUPPORT

8.1 Updates are signed by Karots and installed by the Shop from inside the Software. Karots never
    updates a shop by itself.
8.2 What is free, what is charged, visits, refunds and the shop rules are in the Karots Suite
    Shop Rules & Service Guide given with these terms (the version named in the Order Details). It
    forms part of these terms. The Second Schedule summarises the services.


9. WHAT KAROTS PROMISES

9.1 Karots will supply the Software with reasonable skill and care, and it will work materially
    as its documentation describes on supported computers.
9.2 If it does not, tell Karots in writing. Karots will fix it, work around it or, if it cannot
    within a reasonable time, refund the licence fee for the part that does not work. Bugs
    reported in the first year after installation are fixed free; after that, as the Shop Rules
    & Service Guide says.
9.3 Apart from clause 9 and anything the law does not allow to be excluded, the Software is
    supplied as it is. No other promise is made that it is free of all errors or fits a purpose
    Karots was not told about.
9.4 The Shop remains responsible for checking its own cash, stock, prices, tax returns and
    records, for keeping its computers and backups safe, and for following the laws that apply
    to its trade (for example pharmacy, consumer and tax law).


10. LIABILITY

10.1 Nothing in these terms limits liability for death or personal injury caused by negligence,
     or for fraud (Unfair Contract Terms Act, No. 26 of 1997, section 3(1)).
10.2 Otherwise, neither side is liable for loss of profit, revenue, business or goodwill, or for
     indirect or consequential loss.
10.3 Otherwise, Karots' total liability under these terms in any 12 months is limited to the
     greater of (a) the fees the Shop paid Karots in the 12 months before the claim and
     (b) the amount in the Order Details. Karots sets this limit with regard to its resources and
     the insurance reasonably available to it (Unfair Contract Terms Act, section 10(4)).
10.4 Karots is not liable for loss of Shop Data that a backup the Shop could have restored would
     have avoided.


11. ENDING THESE TERMS

11.1 The Shop may end these terms at any time by stopping use of the Software. Fees already paid
     are refunded only under clause 9.2 or the refund rules in the Shop Rules & Service Guide.
11.2 Karots may end them by written notice if the Shop seriously breaks them (for example clause
     4) and, where the breach can be put right, does not do so within 30 days of being asked, or
     as clause 7.3 says for an unpaid balance.
11.3 When they end, the Shop must stop using the Software and delete it, after taking a final
     backup of its Shop Data (the uninstaller does this first). Clauses 4, 5, 6, 10, 12 and
     the Third Schedule survive.


12. GENERAL

12.1 Governing law: the laws of the Democratic Socialist Republic of Sri Lanka.
12.2 Disputes: the parties will first try to settle a dispute by talking for 30 days. If that
     fails, it goes to arbitration in Colombo under the Arbitration Act, No. 11 of 1995, by a
     single arbitrator agreed by both sides (or, failing agreement, appointed under that Act).
     Either side may still ask a court for urgent relief, such as an injunction against
     copying the Software.
12.3 Notices must be in writing, to the email or address in the Order Details. Karots: the
     contact in clause 12.7.
12.4 Neither side is liable for delay caused by events beyond its reasonable control.
12.5 If a court or arbitrator finds part of these terms unenforceable, the rest stands.
12.6 Karots may change these terms for future updates by giving 30 days' notice. Terms already
     agreed for a version the Shop has do not change without its agreement.
12.7 Karots Korp (Karots Dev) — adhnanmsa@gmail.com — 0769626396.


SECOND SCHEDULE — SERVICES

1. Updates and bug fixes: free for the first year after installation. After that the Shop keeps
   using the version it has, and updates, fixes and help are paid work or a renewal.
2. Support: free remote help in the first year, personalised help free in the first 60 days, and
   2 free visits in the first year, as the Shop Rules & Service Guide sets out. A support session
   uses the Software's rotating support code, which works only for that Shop's install ID, and
   remote access only when the Shop allows it.
3. Karots cloud backup (if in the Order Details): a paid service, monthly or yearly. One encrypted
   copy of the Shop's newest automatic backup about once a day, kept in Karots' storage. If a
   payment is more than 7 days late the service is frozen (no new copies) until it is paid. The
   Shop can switch it off at any time on the Data page. A copy can be brought back on request or
   from the Data page.
4. The Shop's own copy folder (USB, drive or network share) is the Shop's responsibility.


THIRD SCHEDULE — HOW KAROTS HANDLES PERSONAL DATA

1. Karots handles Shop Data only (a) to give support the Shop asks for, (b) to keep the Karots
   cloud backups the Shop has chosen, and (c) as the law requires. It acts only on the Shop's
   instructions and for no purpose of its own.
2. Karots keeps Shop Data confidential and lets only people bound to confidentiality see it.
3. Cloud backups are encrypted with a key for that Shop before they leave the Shop's computer.
   They may be stored with a cloud storage provider whose servers can be outside Sri Lanka. The
   Shop agrees to this, and Karots will meet any conditions the law sets for such transfers.
4. Karots will tell the Shop without undue delay if it learns that Shop Data in its care has been
   lost, disclosed or accessed without authority, and will help the Shop meet its own duties.
5. Karots will help the Shop answer requests from people about their own data, as far as the
   Software and Karots' copies allow.
6. When the services end, Karots deletes its copies of Shop Data, or returns them if the Shop
   asks first. Backup copies held under a deletion lock are deleted when the lock ends.
7. Health data (Pharmacy plugin), identity numbers and similar sensitive data get the same
   protection, and Karots looks at them only when support for that data is asked for.
8. This Schedule is meant to meet the Personal Data Protection Act, No. 9 of 2022 (as amended
   by Act No. 22 of 2025). When that Act's duties for controllers and processors come into
   force, the parties will make any further terms it requires.
